	'cd_h2' => 'What happens if a scheduled collection is missed?',
	'cd_lead' => 'Every collection day follows a verified seven-step timetable from early morning depot departure to digital report delivery. Our structured routine gives site managers complete predictability over their loading bays.',
	'cd_p0' => 'Our daily operation begins at 05:30 with an automated text notice sent to the site facilities manager confirming round dispatch. At 05:45, our vehicles leave the Port Alder depot to begin morning rounds. Driver Rafael Duarte arrives on site for the 06:10 bins out check, verifying bin room access, day tags, and clear passage. At 06:25, the mechanical bin lift commences, securely emptying containers into designated truck compartments before returning each bin to its bay.',
	'cd_p1' => 'At 06:40, if foreign materials are detected inside any container, a contamination photo is recorded before the lift is rescheduled. The vehicle returns to the depot for the 07:40 weigh-in, where certified platform scales log exact payload weights. By 09:00, Priya Nair processes the digital report email, delivering itemised tonnage data and transfer confirmation directly to your inbox. This seven-step timetable maintains complete transparency for multi-tenant buildings and commercial food businesses.',
	'cd_p2' => 'If road blockages or gated access issues prevent a scheduled lift, our missed-pickup rule applies immediately. The missed-pickup line (+00 0000 0418) is answered Monday to Saturday from 06:00 to 18:00 by our customer desk. We schedule a re-collection for the same day or the next working day without delay. Collections operate Monday to Friday between 05:30 and 18:00, with Saturday morning rounds running from 06:00 to 12:00, ensuring your yard remains clear.',
