	'ct_h2' => 'How quickly can collections begin after our site visit?',
	'ct_p0' => 'Establishing your regular service follows four transparent steps: call, visit, schedule, and first lift. First, you contact Ines Lindqvist at our customer desk by telephone or email at desk@meguri-waste.example. Second, Mara Okafor visits your site to audit bin room storage and vehicle access. Third, we establish your fixed weekly timetable, allocate container sizes, and attach day tags. Fourth, your first lift takes place within 10 working days of the site visit. There is no setup fee for sites operating under 8 bins, and contracts remain on a monthly rolling basis with 30 days notice.',
	'ct_p1' => 'Our central operations are located at Unit 4, Quay Road Yard, Port Alder, operating under carrier licence WC-2011-0418. Our collection window runs Monday to Friday from 05:30 to 18:00, with Saturday morning rounds operating from 06:00 to 12:00. The customer desk is staffed Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 17:30 for account support, billing enquiries, and schedule modifications. Our dedicated missed-pickup line (+00 0000 0418) is answered Monday to Saturday from 06:00 to 18:00, providing re-collection on the same or next working day whenever access is blocked.',
	'ct_p2' => 'Your regular scheduled collections begin within 10 working days following Mara Okafor\'s site audit. During this setup period, our depot team prepares your bins, fits colour-coded lids, and prints your customized day tags. Route lead Tomás Ferreira schedules your location into our north or central round to ensure reliable dawn arrival. If you require emergency bins prior to your scheduled start date, our customer desk can arrange delivery from our Port Alder depot.',
	'nl_h0' => 'Operational route notices and timetable updates',
