	'sx_lead' => 'Meguri Waste manages five distinct commercial waste streams on assigned weekly collection days. Every stream uses dedicated container sizes to ensure clean segregation and efficient processing.',
	'sx_out' => 'Stays out',
	'sx_pq' => 'When our route driver identifies non-conforming items inside a container during the pre-lift check, the bin is paused to protect the processing batch. Amina Yusuf, our contamination lead, records photographic evidence and logs the item details. Our customer desk immediately alerts your facilities coordinator with the image and notes. You can choose to remove the non-conforming material before a re-collection lift or request an extra general waste lift.',
	'sx_strip' => 'Panorama of five sorted containers, scroll sideways',
	'sx_t' => 'Commercial Waste Streams',
	'th_back' => 'Back to the home page',
	'th_h0' => 'What to expect next for your site assessment',
	'th_h1' => 'When will our first commercial collection take place?',
	'th_lead' => 'We have received your enquiry and will contact your site coordinator shortly. Our customer desk at Port Alder reviews every request within one business day.',
	'th_p0' => 'Ines Lindqvist from our customer desk will review your facility details and telephone or email your team to schedule a site walk. Mara Okafor will visit your commercial premises to inspect bin storage areas, vehicle clearances, and container requirements. Following the site assessment, we provide a structured collection timetable and container quote based on our transparent weekly tiers. There is no setup fee for sites operating under 8 bins, and agreements remain on rolling monthly terms.',
	'th_p1' => 'Once you approve your collection timetable, your first collection lift takes place within 10 working days of the site visit. Our operations team prepares your four-wheel 660 L bins or 240 L consoles, attaches weather-resistant day tags, and places your site on Tomás Ferreira\'s morning route. For any urgent operational questions, our customer desk is available Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 17:30, or you can email desk@meguri-waste.example.',
	'th_t' => 'Thank You for Contacting Meguri Waste',
	'tm_h0' => 'Service agreements and rolling terms',
	'tm_h1' => 'What are customer responsibilities for bin access and contamination?',
	'tm_lead' => 'These terms govern commercial waste collection services provided by Meguri Waste from our Port Alder depot. All services are subject to these conditions alongside individual service level agreements.',
	'tm_p0' => 'Commercial collections are supplied on a monthly rolling contract basis requiring 30 days written notice for termination or service adjustment. There are no setup fees for commercial sites operating with fewer than 8 bins. Standard pricing plans include Starter at €48/week, Core at €96/week, and Full week at €158/week, with optional Food daily add-ons at €34/week, extra lifts at €22/lift, and confidential consoles at €14/month. All charges are denominated in EUR, ex VAT, and billed monthly. First collection commences within 10 working days of completed site assessment.',
	'tm_p1' => 'Customers must ensure collection containers are accessible during scheduled collection windows (Monday to Friday 05:30 to 18:00, Saturday 06:00 to 12:00). Gates, bin stores, and loading docks must remain unlocked and unobstructed. Materials deposited into each container must comply strictly with assigned stream definitions. Where non-conforming items or hazardous materials are identified, Meguri Waste reserves the right to pause collection and provide photographic evidence. Missed collections caused by access blockages will be re-serviced on the same or next working day once reported to our missed-pickup line (+00 0000 0418).',
	'tm_t' => 'Terms of Service',
	'wc_h0' => 'Commercial pricing tiers and optional add-ons',
	'wc_h1' => 'What is included in every weekly agreement',
	'wc_h2' => 'How does the monthly rolling contract work?',
	'wc_i1' => 'Four-wheel containers with colour-coded lids',
	'wc_i2' => 'Weather-resistant day tags on every bin',
	'wc_i3' => 'On-site audit before the first delivery',
	'wc_i4' => 'Weighbridge certificate emailed by 09:00',
	'wc_lead' => 'Meguri Waste provides predictable weekly commercial waste plans billed on a simple monthly rolling agreement. Every package includes dedicated bins, day tags, and verified digital weighbridge reporting.',
	'wc_p0' => 'Our standard pricing covers six clearly defined tiers and add-ons in EUR, ex VAT. The Starter plan covers 1 stream with one 660 L bin weekly at €48/week. The Core plan provides comprehensive coverage across 3 streams at €96/week. The Full week package covers all 5 streams at €158/week. For commercial kitchens and hospitality venues, the Food daily add-on provides 3 lifts/week at €34/week. Additional unscheduled collections can be booked as an Extra lift for any stream at €22/lift. Secure documentation handling is available with a 240 L Confidential console including fortnightly shred at €14/month.',
	'wc_p1' => 'Every scheduled collection agreement includes clean four-wheel containers, colour-coded lids, and durable weather-resistant day tags. Mara Okafor completes an on-site audit to measure loading access and bin room capacity before delivery. Automated morning dispatch texts keep facilities teams informed, while digital weighbridge certificates are emailed by 09:00 following each collection. Customer support is provided directly by Ines Lindqvist at our customer desk, available Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 17:30 to assist with schedule adjustments and regulatory transfer documentation.',
	'wc_p2' => 'All Meguri Waste agreements operate on a straightforward monthly rolling basis requiring only 30 days notice to amend or cancel. We do not lock commercial sites into multi-year tie-ins. Furthermore, there is no setup fee for sites operating under 8 bins. Site assessments are completed within days of initial contact, and your first lift takes place within 10 working days of the site visit. All listed prices are billed in EUR, ex VAT, on consistent monthly itemised statements.',
	'wc_t' => 'Weekly Cover & Pricing',
	'pg_contact_lead' => 'Setting up commercial waste collection with Meguri Waste follows four simple steps. We assess your site in person and establish your regular weekly collections within 10 working days.',
	'pg_newsletter_lead' => 'Collection Notes is Meguri Waste\'s email bulletin for commercial facilities managers and site coordinators. Subscribe to receive route-day notices, holiday timetable shifts, and direct depot service updates.',
);
